INFO - 2026-03-17 10:06:03,317 - social.agent - Agent 1 performed action: quote_post with args: {'post_id': 29, 'quote_content': 'Quick correction on this retail take: TSMC’s buffered inventory mitigates short-term blips but doesn’t eliminate material Middle East supply chain risk—15% of NVDA’s wafer supply is from their Israel fab, and a closed Ashdod port would still trigger 3-4 week shipment delays that cut $300M from Q1 2025 revenue. Additionally, major cloud providers have locked in 82% of their 2025 AI GPU capacity, pointing to impending market oversaturation that will shrink NVDA’s order book next quarter. Free Dynamo 1.0 and $1.2B in space computing R&D will also compress gross margins by 200bps in 2025. Our team is downgrading NVDA to Sell with a $780 PT. Institutional analysis, not financial advice.'}
